    id 92
    label "bJw3s85EcxM"
    step 0
    date "2013-01-20T03:57:10Z"
    title "Transgender at 11: Listening to Jazz Jennings | 20/20 | ABC News"
    description "Barbara Walters catches up with Jazz Jennings, a young girl who says she was born in the wrong body. After being diagnosed with gender dysphoria at age 5, Jazz began living as a transgender girl and has officially transitioned from male to female. &amp;#10;SUBSCRIBE for the latest news and updates from ABC News &amp;#9658; http://www.youtube.com/subscription_center?add_user=abcnews &amp;#10;To read the full story and others, visit http://www.abcnews.com &amp;#10;&amp;#10;Watch more news stories from ABC News!&amp;#10;Transgender &amp;#9658; https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pjKBnFtmKKA&amp;#38;list=PLQOa26lW-uI-UfMJv2hQ5m2qJL00wxwYl&amp;#38;index=7&amp;#10;Parenting  &amp;#9658; https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5dJduGC3HyQ&amp;#38;list=PLQOa26lW-uI9vaLCJEngtgEk8w3MI7Sfr&amp;#38;index=4&amp;#10;&amp;#10;On the surface, the Jennings and their four children are a typical American family. But when &amp;#34;20/20&amp;#34; first interviewed them, their youngest child, a kindergartener named Jazz, was already one of the youngest known cases of an early transition from male to female.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;From the moment he could speak, Jazz made it clear he wanted to wear a dress. At only 15 months, he would unsnap his onesies to make it look like a dress. When his parents praised Jazz as a &amp;#34;good boy,&amp;#34; he would correct them, saying he was a good girl.&amp;#10;--To read the full story and others, visit http://www.abcnews.com&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Follow ABC News across the web!&amp;#10;Facebook: http://www.facebook.com/abcnews &amp;#10;Twitter: http://twitter.com/ABC&amp;#10;Instagram: https://instagram.com/ABCNews/ &amp;#10;&amp;#10;The LGBTQ community is becoming a more vocal minority, looking for equal treatment on issues from marriage equality to anti-discrimination in the workplace. Watch stories about how the lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, and queer population aims to address stigma, discrimination and prejudice. See stories of hate crimes, health disparities, and violence against their marginalized groups. Turn to ABC News for the latest gay news, breaking stories on transgenders, and discussions on gender dysphoria. Join the discussion and find more about issues of sexual orientation, gender inequality and gender identity. Stay up to date with these videos and view all photos and more with with ABC News.  &amp;#10;&amp;#10;20/20 , with the help of Elizabeth Vargas and David Muir, combines hard hitting investigative reports, compelling human interest pieces, and newsmaker interviews. A staple of primetime television on Friday nights for over 3 decades, 20/20 has remained a leader in American TV news magazines broadcasting on ABC. The in-depth story packages can be seen Friday nights at 10|9c.&amp;#10;&amp;#10;Make ABC News your daily news outlet for breaking national and world news, broadcast video coverage, and exclusive interviews that will help you stay up to date on the events shaping our world. ABC News&amp;#8217; show roster has both leaders in daily evening and morning programming. Kick start your weekday mornings with news updates from Good Morning America (GMA) and Sundays with This Week with George Stephanopoulos. Get your evening fix with 20/20, Nightline, and ABC World News Tonight with David Muir. Head to abc.go.com for programming schedule and more information on ABC News."
